From 24334930cac802523153307b493cde1a20a0420b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:05:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Draw an arrow cursor while the UI is hidden (F10)

The client draws its mouse cursor from the window manager's DrawWindows(),
which is skipped when the UI is hidden (screen mode 3), so the cursor
disappears even though the mouse still works for clicking mobs in the
world. The newer eqw.dll also calls SetCursor(NULL) over the game window,
so the Windows cursor cannot just be re-enabled.

Add a small HideUiCursor class that draws a flat white arrow with a black
border at the client's mouse position from the RenderUI callback, using
transformed vertices (no texture asset). Scaled from 20 px at 1080p with
the screen height. It is only drawn in game, with the UI hidden, while
the game window has focus and not during right mouse button mouse look.

New setting ShowCursorWithUiHidden ([Zeal] ini section), on by default,
toggled with /uicursor [on|off]. Documented in the README.

No options window checkbox yet: that needs new XML in both uifiles/zeal
and uifiles/zeal/big_xml.
